[{:db/id "q-3946/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "73d6f39b-91f0-5dea-b230-6cbac64088e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3946/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" :answer/id #uuid "66737e74-d6a6-58ce-8d9f-dabf599435ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3946/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "7543d9d8-5714-590a-bc8a-a6a9d62fb853" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3946/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "be702a1d-6741-5945-b020-3f09e397ecec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3946/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" :answer/id #uuid "166da29f-830c-51f1-872d-85cfc1bb508a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3946/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b06e830-db73-555b-8e8e-61bcf09f61fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-3946/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-3946/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-3946/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" "q-3946/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" "q-3946/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-3946/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3946" :question/id #uuid "494506ed-3be9-5fa5-a304-e992bf8e5303" :question/math-academy-id "q-3946" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(4{x}^{2}-5x+16).$" :question/worked-solution "We identify the leading term and compute its limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(4{x}^{2}-5x+16) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\infty \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-3946/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc04f720-28f3-55ab-8e89-582db57672a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3946"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35241/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" :answer/id #uuid "1be6bff0-5372-5728-ac3d-51d12660551e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186103763 :answer-field/choices ["q-35241/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35241"] :question/worked-solution "Applying the power rule and the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{(xf(x))}^{3} & =({lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3})\\cdot ({lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)^{3}) \\\\  & =({lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3})\\cdot {({lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x))}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=3.$ Therefore, the above becomes:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{(xf(x))}^{3} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3}\\cdot {(3)}^{3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3}\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =27\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph $y={x}^{3}$ is power function with an odd positive power and therefore has the property that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3}=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nMultiplication by the positive constant $27$ does not affect the limit at infinity. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{(xf(x))}^{3}=-\\infty .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-99300/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "f4d78422-761c-5dd6-b0ee-a4dfe3f5ab5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99300/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" :answer/id #uuid "1d6f6749-6e90-5d9e-8c94-680278bcb57b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99300/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "46e4413e-1007-561a-93c7-561b7005cc4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99300/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" :answer/id #uuid "34b0d2ff-47c9-50a0-b61d-b991e370d1aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99300/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "59e2b2c6-ef9d-511e-a415-54c21f1f28c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99300/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7beb79b6-a8a5-5e99-91e8-88fbe9740b9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-99300/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-99300/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-99300/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" "q-99300/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" "q-99300/selection/c5e624c1da93ecfedccf3fa70b8e1fb64de1e5d703dcc02fa7b4793f81a70f81" "q-99300/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-99300" :question/id #uuid "7b459699-7d1d-5e8e-a709-c8342eddf28d" :question/math-academy-id "q-99300" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{({t}^{2}+1)}^{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "We identify the leading term and compute its limit. In this case, we raise the main term of the base polynomial to the given power.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }({t}^{2}+1)^{4} & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }({t}^{2})^{4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{t}^{8} \\\\  & =\\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-99300/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc04f720-28f3-55ab-8e89-582db57672a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99300"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-300764/field-1/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "801ae9f6-4a13-5b1a-b819-e5b015026f91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-300764/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec6c42cf-3de2-5c62-a967-ccb826434ed8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-300764/field-1/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer-field/choices ["q-300764/field-1/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-300764" :question/id #uuid "1336bf1c-c2e9-5332-8785-2d27b64acedf" :question/math-academy-id "q-300764" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $p(x)=-3{x}^{5}$ and $q(x)=\\frac{4}{{x}^{7}}$, then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{2}\\cdot p(x)\\cdot q(x))=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's calculate ${x}^{2}\\cdot p(x):$\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}\\cdot p(x)={x}^{2}\\cdot (-3{x}^{5})=-3{x}^{7}\n$$\n\nWhen we multiply the two functions ${x}^{2}\\cdot p(x)$ and $q(x)$, we get a constant, and the limit of a constant is just the constant itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{2}\\cdot p(x)\\cdot q(x)) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(-3{x}^{7}\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{7}}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }-12 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-300764/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6456693-8845-5f7b-8b0b-2d6802bbf72e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-300764"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336931/field-1/2d8ae85212023567913a414489d5205c33db213bce0e85f85a24e6dff779b8a6" :answer/id #uuid "c3685cc7-ddff-5482-8916-b374a64f49d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336931/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c6e28e5-0291-5836-94b7-dac8034cab72" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336931/field-1/2d8ae85212023567913a414489d5205c33db213bce0e85f85a24e6dff779b8a6" :answer-field/choices ["q-336931/field-1/2d8ae85212023567913a414489d5205c33db213bce0e85f85a24e6dff779b8a6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336931" :question/id #uuid "b7051329-a00a-5962-876e-9ade482c493a" :question/math-academy-id "q-336931" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $p(x)=11{x}^{4}$ and $q(x)=5{x}^{4},$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{p(x)}{q(x)}=$  \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "When we divide the two functions, we get a constant, and the limit of a constant is just the constant itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{p(x)}{q(x)} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(11{x}^{4})}{(5{x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{11}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336931/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6456693-8845-5f7b-8b0b-2d6802bbf72e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336931"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
